l education began within the family. Learning began before children entered formal places of study. Life skills. Children learnt activities such as farming and fishing. Adults guided children through everyday experiences. Craft skills. Woodworking and handicrafts formed part of learning. These skills were connected to the needs of family life. Adult guidance. Families and communities passed on knowledge. Children learnt through demonstration and practice. Preparation for life. Learning helped children become independent as adults. The aim was to prepare them for independence in adulthood."}